§§ `General Condition 4`

`a fraudulent claim` MEANS
    `a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of` (LIST (`a damaged` buildings `by` (LIST `directly` fire))) `with theft` NOTHING `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` (`conduct with` (LIST `a fraudulent claim`) `and` `the procedure followed`) `premium` `the premium paid on time`

#ASSERT `why General Condition 4(a) forfeits the benefits` `a fraudulent claim` EQUALS LIST "General Condition 4(a): the claim is fraudulent in some respect"
#ASSERT `why General Condition 4(a) forfeits the benefits` (`a loss of the item` (`a damaged` buildings `by` (LIST `directly` fire))) EQUALS EMPTY

-- (b): rejected 15 March 2026; three calendar months end 15 June (fork F29)
#ASSERT `the last day to commence proceedings, three months from` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 15
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 4(b) has forfeited the benefits` (YMD 2026 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 15)) (YMD 2026 9 1)
#ASSERT `General Condition 4(b) has forfeited the benefits` (YMD 2026 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 16)) (YMD 2026 9 1)
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 4(b) has forfeited the benefits` (YMD 2026 3 15) NOTHING (YMD 2026 6 15)
#ASSERT `General Condition 4(b) has forfeited the benefits` (YMD 2026 3 15) NOTHING (YMD 2026 6 16)
-- the month-end: three months from 30 November end on the last day of February
#ASSERT `the last day to commence proceedings, three months from` (YMD 2026 11 30) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28

§§ `General Condition 7: the second arbitrator (clock in months)`

-- appointed at one month: too early, a nullity; the duty stays live
#TRACE `General Condition 7: appointing the second arbitrator` `the Insured` `the Insurer` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `appoint an arbitrator in writing` AT 1
-- appointed at exactly two months: the only day that complies
#TRACE `General Condition 7: appointing the second arbitrator` `the Insured` `the Insurer` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `appoint an arbitrator in writing` AT 2
-- appointed at three months: late; the other party may appoint a sole arbitrator
#TRACE `General Condition 7: appointing the second arbitrator` `the Insured` `the Insurer` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `appoint an arbitrator in writing` AT 3

§§ `General Condition 8`

GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `A change affecting the item`
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`the burnt building after` cs MEANS `A damaged item` WITH
    `the item insured`                  IS `the building`
    `kind`                              IS buildings
    `the chain of causation`            IS LIST (`directly` fire)
    `circumstances`                     IS `the ordinary circumstances`
    `valuation`                         IS `the ordinary valuation`
    `what the Insured told the Insurer` IS `nothing false was said`
    `changes under General Condition 8` IS cs
    `claimed as a cost of changing or adding to a computer system, programme, software or chip` IS FALSE

GIVEN c IS A `A change under General Condition 8`
      a IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A change affecting the item`
`the change` c `accepted` a MEANS `A change affecting the item` WITH `the change` IS c, `accepted by endorsement before the loss` IS a

`the GC 8 reason` MEANS LIST "General Condition 8: the policy had ceased to attach to the property after a change the Insurer had not accepted"

-- (b): 29 days unattended, no; 30 days, yes ("từ 30 ngày trở lên"); 30 days accepted by endorsement, no
#ASSERT `why General Condition 8 takes the item out` (`the burnt building after` (LIST (`the change` (`the building or premises left unattended` 29) `accepted` FALSE))) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `why General Condition 8 takes the item out` (`the burnt building after` (LIST (`the change` (`the building or premises left unattended` 30) `accepted` FALSE))) EQUALS `the GC 8 reason`
#ASSERT `why General Condition 8 takes the item out` (`the burnt building after` (LIST (`the change` (`the building or premises left unattended` 30) `accepted` TRUE))) EQUALS EMPTY
-- (a), first limb, needs no increase of risk (fork F22)
#ASSERT `why General Condition 8 takes the item out` (`the burnt building after` (LIST (`the change` `a change of the Insured's business or manufacture` `accepted` FALSE))) EQUALS `the GC 8 reason`
-- (c)
#ASSERT `why General Condition 8 takes the item out` (`the burnt building after` (LIST (`the change` `removal to a place this policy does not cover` `accepted` FALSE))) EQUALS `the GC 8 reason`
-- (d): a sale, yes; an inheritance, no
#ASSERT `why General Condition 8 takes the item out` (`the burnt building after` (LIST (`the change` (`a transfer of the Insured's interest` FALSE) `accepted` FALSE))) EQUALS `the GC 8 reason`
#ASSERT `why General Condition 8 takes the item out` (`the burnt building after` (LIST (`the change` (`a transfer of the Insured's interest` TRUE) `accepted` FALSE))) EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `General Condition 9`

-- (b): 30 days, or a longer period agreed in writing
#ASSERT `the days allowed for the written claim under` `the procedure followed` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the days allowed for the written claim under` (`a claims procedure with` (JUST 40) (JUST 45) TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 45
#ASSERT `the days allowed for the written claim under` (`a claims procedure with` (JUST 40) (JUST 20) TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 30

GIVEN cp IS A `The claims procedure as performed`
GIVETH A `A loss`
`a fire claim made with` cp MEANS
    `a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of` (LIST (`a damaged` buildings `by` (LIST `directly` fire))) `with theft` NOTHING `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` (`conduct with` EMPTY `and` cp) `premium` `the premium paid on time`

GIVEN cp IS A `The claims procedure as performed`
GIVETH A `A loss`
`a burglary claim made with` cp MEANS
    `a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of` (LIST (`a damaged` stock `by` (LIST `directly` theft))) `with theft` (JUST (`The circumstances of a theft` WITH `in the insured building` IS TRUE, `with force or violence to break in or to get out` IS TRUE)) `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` (`conduct with` EMPTY `and` cp) `premium` `the premium paid on time`

-- day 30 is in time, day 31 is not; day 40 is in time where 45 were agreed; no claim at all is not
#ASSERT `why General Condition 9 is not met` (`a fire claim made with` (`a claims procedure with` (JUST 30) NOTHING TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `why General Condition 9 is not met` (`a fire claim made with` (`a claims procedure with` (JUST 31) NOTHING TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS LIST "General Condition 9(b)(i): no written claim within the period"
#ASSERT `why General Condition 9 is not met` (`a fire claim made with` (`a claims procedure with` (JUST 40) (JUST 45) TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `why General Condition 9 is not met` (`a fire claim made with` (`a claims procedure with` NOTHING NOTHING TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS LIST "General Condition 9(b)(i): no written claim within the period"
-- (a)(i), (ii): not immediate
#ASSERT `why General Condition 9 is not met` (`a fire claim made with` (`a claims procedure with` (JUST 10) NOTHING FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS LIST "General Condition 9(a)(i): no immediate measures to minimise the loss", "General Condition 9(a)(ii): no immediate written notice to the Insurer"
-- (a)(iii): the police must be told of a theft, and need not be told of a fire
#ASSERT `General Condition 9 requires the police to be notified of` (`a burglary claim made with` `the procedure followed`)
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 9 requires the police to be notified of` (`a fire claim made with` `the procedure followed`)
#ASSERT `why General Condition 9 is not met` (`a burglary claim made with` (`a claims procedure with` (JUST 10) NOTHING TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS LIST "General Condition 9(a)(iii): the police were not notified immediately"
#ASSERT `why General Condition 9 is not met` (`a fire claim made with` (`a claims procedure with` (JUST 10) NOTHING TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS EMPTY

-- The duties as obligations (clock in days from awareness). "Immediately" is taken as the same
-- day (0) for these traces only: a scenario value, not the document's (fork F17).
#TRACE `General Condition 9: the Insured's duties` 0 FALSE 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `take all necessary measures to minimise the loss and recover lost property` AT 0
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `notify the Insurer in writing` AT 0
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `submit a written claim listing the items and amounts` AT 30
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `give particulars of other insurances` AT 30
#TRACE `General Condition 9: the Insured's duties` 0 FALSE 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `take all necessary measures to minimise the loss and recover lost property` AT 0
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `notify the Insurer in writing` AT 1
#TRACE `General Condition 9: the Insured's duties` 0 FALSE 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `take all necessary measures to minimise the loss and recover lost property` AT 0
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `notify the Insurer in writing` AT 0
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `give particulars of other insurances` AT 20
    PARTY `the Insured` DOES `submit a written claim listing the items and amounts` AT 31

§§ `General Conditions 5, 10, 11, 12, 13`

GIVEN ls IS A LIST OF `A lapse`
GIVETH A `A loss`
`a fire claim with the lapses` ls MEANS
    `a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of` (LIST (`a damaged` buildings `by` (LIST `directly` fire))) `with theft` NOTHING `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` (`conduct with` ls `and` `the procedure followed`) `premium` `the premium paid on time`

#ASSERT `why General Condition 5 is not met` (`a fire claim with the lapses` (LIST `refusing subrogation`)) EQUALS LIST "General Condition 5: the Insured refused an act the Insurer required against third parties"
#ASSERT `why General Condition 10 forfeits the benefits` (`a fire claim with the lapses` (LIST `hindering the Insurer`)) EQUALS LIST "General Condition 10: the Insured hindered the Insurer in exercising its powers"
#ASSERT `why General Condition 11 is not met` (`a fire claim with the lapses` (LIST `withholding reinstatement plans`)) EQUALS LIST "General Condition 11: the plans and information required for the reinstatement were not provided"
#ASSERT `why General Condition 12 is not met` (`a fire claim with the lapses` (LIST `a precaution not taken`)) EQUALS LIST "General Condition 12: not every precaution to prevent loss was taken"
#ASSERT `why General Condition 13 is not met` (`a fire claim with the lapses` (LIST `insuring the deductible`)) EQUALS LIST "General Condition 13: the Insured insured the deductible elsewhere"
#ASSERT `why the general conditions defeat the claim` `the Schedule` (`a fire claim with the lapses` EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY
-- General Condition 10: the powers last until the Insured disclaims, or the claim is decided or withdrawn
#ASSERT `the Insurer may still exercise its General Condition 10 rights` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Insurer may still exercise its General Condition 10 rights` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Insurer may still exercise its General Condition 10 rights` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Insured may abandon property to the Insurer`

§§ `General Condition 15`

-- a period of 365 days: (a)(i), 30 days from acceptance on 1 January 2026, so 31 January
#ASSERT `the period of insurance in days` `the Schedule` EQUALS 365
#ASSERT `General Condition 15: the last day to pay the premium` `the Schedule` `the premium paid on time` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
-- paid on the last day: the cover stands for a loss in June
#ASSERT `General Condition 15 leaves the cover in force for a loss on` `the Schedule` (`the premium paid on` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 31))) (YMD 2026 6 1)
-- paid a day late: the cover was cancelled, and a June loss is not covered
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 15 leaves the cover in force for a loss on` `the Schedule` (`the premium paid on` (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1))) (YMD 2026 6 1)
-- never paid: a loss within the warranty period is still covered (clause 2, fork F27); a loss after it is not
#ASSERT `General Condition 15 leaves the cover in force for a loss on` `the Schedule` (`the premium paid on` NOTHING) (YMD 2026 1 31)
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 15 leaves the cover in force for a loss on` `the Schedule` (`the premium paid on` NOTHING) (YMD 2026 2 1)

GIVEN f IS A DATE
      t IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The Schedule`
`a Schedule for the period` f `to` t MEANS `The Schedule` WITH
    `policy number`                                     IS "TEST-2"
    `the period of insurance`                           IS `A period` WITH `first day` IS f, `last day` IS t
    `renewal periods paid for and accepted`             IS EMPTY
    `the items`                                         IS LIST `the building`
    `the total sum insured`                             IS 1000000000
    `already paid under this policy in the period`      IS 0
    `the limits of liability`                           IS EMPTY
    `the deductible for each loss`                      IS NOTHING
    `the annual premium`                                IS 12000000
    `the premium for the period`                        IS 1000000
    `the Insured has paid or agreed to pay the premium` IS TRUE

-- a period of exactly 30 days is (a): 30 days from acceptance; one of 29 days is (c): within the period (fork F26)
#ASSERT `the period of insurance in days` (`a Schedule for the period` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 1 30)) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `General Condition 15: the last day to pay the premium` (`a Schedule for the period` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 1 30)) `the premium paid on time` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `General Condition 15: the last day to pay the premium` (`a Schedule for the period` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 1 29)) `the premium paid on time` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 29

-- instalments: the first within 30 days; a later one missed on 1 July ends the cover after that day
`instalments, the July one missed` MEANS `The premium payment` WITH
    `the Insurer accepted payment by instalments`                IS TRUE
    `date the cover was accepted`                                IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `date the premium was paid in full`                          IS JUST (YMD 2026 1 20)
    `agreed date of the first later instalment not paid on time` IS JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT `General Condition 15 leaves the cover in force for a loss on` `the Schedule` `instalments, the July one missed` (YMD 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 15 leaves the cover in force for a loss on` `the Schedule` `instalments, the July one missed` (YMD 2026 7 2)

-- endorsements: 30 days from the later of the day the cover takes effect and the day of issue
#ASSERT `General Condition 15: the last day to pay the premium for` (`An endorsement` WITH `date the cover in it takes effect` IS YMD 2026 5 1, `date it was issued` IS YMD 2026 4 20) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 31
#ASSERT `General Condition 15: the last day to pay the premium for` (`An endorsement` WITH `date the cover in it takes effect` IS YMD 2026 4 1, `date it was issued` IS YMD 2026 4 20) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 20
#ASSERT `General Condition 15: the last day to pay the premium for` (`An endorsement` WITH `date the cover in it takes effect` IS YMD 2026 4 20, `date it was issued` IS YMD 2026 4 20) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 20
